      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "Copyright © 2015 Elsevier Inc. All rights reserved.",
        "AbstractText": "Cardiogoniometry is an electrocardiographic and vectorcardiographic method utilizing computer-assisted analysis of cardiac potentials focusing on T-wave abnormalities resulting from myocardial malperfusion. We describe a case of diagnosis of obstructive coronary artery disease with this method and discuss the possible implications for the clinical setting."
      },
